%description:
Test that dropAndDelete() on an object owned by a cSoftOwner (here: the module)
removes the object from the owner's list of owned objects.

dropAndDelete() used to only set the object's owner pointer to nullptr before
deleting it, leaving a dangling pointer in the cSoftOwner's object list,
which caused a crash when the list was traversed later.

%activity:
int n = getNumOwnedObjects();
cMessage *msg = new cMessage("msg");
EV << "added: " << getNumOwnedObjects() - n << endl;
dropAndDelete(msg);
EV << "after dropAndDelete: " << getNumOwnedObjects() - n << endl;

// touch all owned objects -- this would crash on a dangling pointer
for (int i = 0; i < getNumOwnedObjects(); i++)
    (void)getOwnedObject(i)->getClassName();
EV << "done\n";

%contains: stdout
added: 1
after dropAndDelete: 0
done
